From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Gazelka <andrew.gazelka@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 18:11:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nix: add 'nix store builds' command

Adds `nix store builds`, which reports what Nix is currently building
or substituting, and why, without connecting to a daemon: it reads the
coordinators' `graph-<pid>.json` files directly (pruning files whose
recorded pid is dead, since a crashed coordinator cannot clean up).

The default (and `--json`) view is a flat list derived from the graph
files: one entry per running goal, with the why-chain recomputed by
walking the graph's `waiters` edges up to the requested root. With
`--graph`, the command reports each coordinator's goal graph whole,
including waiting and completed goals, as an indented forest or, with
`--json`, as a `{"coordinators": [...]}` document.

Gated on the `build-status-dir` experimental feature, enforced
explicitly in `run()` because the multi-command dispatcher does not
enforce a subcommand's advertised feature automatically.

Refs indexable-inc/index#2485
Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

